arnation she's having the comics  you know maybe her skin would be green  maybe she'd have like the vines actually  coming out of her you know it's sort of  edged across just like one of those  looks one of the more one of the less  human looks and they just kind of didn't  and mio well there's there's a wasted  opportunity plus the fact that I'm stuck  with this one now as far as what happens  to Selena I have mixed feelings about  where when I saw where it was heading I  was like I don't like this at all the  way it actually played out was slightly  better than out then what I was afraid  of I still don't really like it though  so here's my big problem with this with  the whole with the whole premise  apparently now being that this seed is  going to not only help  Selena recover but also sort of bring  out her worst elements to set her up to  be a villain form you know the proper  world of Batman where she'll be Catwoman  and all that um you know I get that but  here's what I don't like about it Bruce  was the one who sought it out Bruce was  the one who brought it back to her Bruce  was honestly the only one who was told  in any terms even the vague ones that he  got what the consequences were gonna be  in other words Selina kind of got robbed  of agency here in turn and I don't just  mean in the immediate because yes she  doesn't make the decision I want to take  it but like this is going to affect the  entire path of her future life and I  feel like in some ways that Rob's her of  the agency of dis of who she gets to  decide to be and that bugs me especially  because I like this version of Selina  and I would have bought this version of  so I was like I would have bought that  there could have been an event where  this version of Selina would have simply  chosen to not walk the straight and  narrow as Bruce does and feeling like  it's it's more forced onto her I don't  like that as a general premise again  it's not as bad as it could have been  cuz she does say